timestamp: 2026-08-26T13:14:00+02:00
operation: connect canonical server path to private M1 GitHub repository
result: stopped before clone

error:
  GitHub returned "Repository not found" during the read-only ls-remote
  validation for Tausendunde1nz/adult-publishing-core.

cause:
  The existing chatops SSH identities are repository-scoped deploy keys. The
  github.com-infra alias authenticates as Tausendunde1nz/infra and the default
  github.com identity authenticates as Tausendunde1nz/docs. Neither key has
  access to the newly created private repository.

impact:
  The private GitHub repository exists with an initial main commit. No local
  /opt/tu1nz_repos/adult-publishing-core path was created and no existing SSH
  key, config, service or repository was changed by the failed validation.

required resolution:
  Create a dedicated Ed25519 deploy key for adult-publishing-core, store the
  private key only under the allowed /etc/tu1nz security path, grant that public
  key read/write access only to Tausendunde1nz/adult-publishing-core, and bind
  the cloned repository to that identity through its local Git configuration.

security gate:
  Key generation and the GitHub deploy-key grant create persistent repository
  access. They require an explicit action-time approval before execution.

rollback:
  Remove the dedicated deploy key from the GitHub repository, remove only its
  dedicated private/public key files, and remove the repository-local SSH
  command. Existing Infra and Docs identities remain untouched.
